<title>AUSTRALIA: Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - May 14.</title>
<headline>Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - May 14.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Tuesday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name			P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	352.53    7.65</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	  231.25    1.11</p>
<p> 3   Ranger Minerals     193.78    4.05</p>
<p> 4   Perilya Mines	 193.02    0.83</p>
<p> 5   Syd Hrbr Casino     150.00    2.22</p>
<p> 6   Equatorial Min	133.33    0.24</p>
<p> 7   Westpac Prop Tr     106.25    1.70</p>
<p> 8   St.Barbara Mine	91.55    0.65</p>
<p> 9   Tap Oil		  80.11    1.41</p>
<p>10   Consol Paper	   77.06    2.62</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining	   2.12    1.05</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	   4.46    1.00</p>
<p> 3   Jardine Fm China	5.10    0.76</p>
<p> 4   BTR Plc		   5.80    5.40</p>
<p> 5   Premier Inv	     5.94    1.40</p>
<p> 6   BT Aust Eq Mgmt	 7.33    0.74</p>
<p> 7   FAI Life ltd	    7.45    0.74</p>
<p> 8   Adel Bton Cement	7.64    1.83</p>
<p> 9   Renison Goldflds	7.66    5.22</p>
<p>10   OLS Asia Hldgs	  7.69    1.10</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
